# This file lists the environment variables each backend reads, one block per backend. You bring
# your own vendor keys, which is what BYO-key means throughout this repo. OpenReading stores none
# of them. Treat this file as a reference list rather than a template. Never run
# `cp .env.example .env`. Add one line per key you hold:
#
#     echo 'REDUCTO_API_KEY=sk_...' >> .env
#
# `.env` is in this repo's .gitignore, so a file written inside a clone is not committed. Your
# shell history still records that line in plain text, in ~/.zsh_history or ~/.bash_history. Type
# the line into an editor instead when the history file matters. Then run `chmod 600 .env`, since
# the usual umask leaves a new file readable by every account on the machine.
#
# Copying changes which backend reads your document. QWEN_VL_ENDPOINT and DOCLING_SERVE_URL below
# ship with a value rather than blank, so a copy marks docling and qwen-vl configured on a machine
# where neither is running. Under a `require_local` policy the router then sends your scan to
# http://localhost:5001, and the response records `docling TerminalError (ConnectError)`. Without
# the copy it records `docling skipped (missing_credentials)` and the document never reaches a
# socket.
#
# OpenReading never writes a key anywhere and never keeps one between calls. The credential broker
# (`openreading.credentials`) reads each key from this process's environment at request time, and
# the charge lands on your own account with the vendor. The CLI loads `.env` on every invocation,
# `openreading serve` included, and never overrides a variable the shell already exports. A Python
# call loads it only when you pass `env_file=`. That module documents the full resolution order,
# the per-backend table and what happens when a key is missing.
#
# An OPENREADING_<SLUG>_<KEY> form beats the service-native var below (the full order is in
# `uv run python -m pydoc openreading.credentials`), so OPENREADING_REDUCTO_API_KEY beats
# REDUCTO_API_KEY. pymupdf and tesseract need no key, because both run on your own machine.

# --- reducto (signup: https://platform.reducto.ai) ---
REDUCTO_API_KEY=
REDUCTO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=                 # Svix signing secret, only for inbound webhooks

# --- chunkr (signup: https://chunkr.ai) ---
CHUNKR_API_KEY=
CHUNKR_BASE_URL=                        # optional: self-hosted (AGPL) container, e.g.
#                                       #   http://localhost:8000

# --- pulse (signup: https://www.runpulse.com) ---
PULSE_API_KEY=

# --- nuextract (signup: https://nuextract.ai, the vendor SDK's NUMIND_API_KEY also works) ---
NUEXTRACT_API_KEY=
NUEXTRACT_BASE_URL=                     # optional: self-hosted NuExtract platform,
#                                       #   default nuextract.ai

# --- open-ocr (signup: https://open-ocr.com, OCR aggregator, billed per page to your balance) ---
OPENOCR_API_KEY=
OPENOCR_ENGINE=                         # optional: engine id, default openocr/tesseract

# --- anthropic-claude (signup: https://console.anthropic.com) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=                        # optional, default claude-opus-4-8

# --- google-gemini (signup: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=                           # optional, default gemini-3.6-flash

# --- mistral-ocr (signup: https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys) ---
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_OCR_MODEL=                      # optional, default mistral-ocr-latest

# --- aws-textract (signup: https://aws.amazon.com/textract/, BYO IAM, billed to your account) ---
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=                      # optional, only for STS/temporary credentials
AWS_REGION=                             # e.g. us-east-1, unset uses the boto3 chain
#                                       #   (AWS_DEFAULT_REGION is also honored)
OPENREADING_TEXTRACT_S3_BUCKET=         # required only for the multi-page async `poll` flow
#                                       #   (sync is 1 page, async up to 3000 pages via S3)

# --- azure-document-intelligence (signup: https://azure.microsoft.com/products/ai-services/ai-document-intelligence) ---
AZURE_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE_ENDPOINT=
AZURE_DOCUMENT_INTELLIGENCE_KEY=

# --- google-document-ai (signup: https://cloud.google.com/document-ai, BYO GCP project + ADC) ---
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=         # path to a service-account JSON (ADC)
GCP_PROJECT_ID=                         # GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT is also honored
GCP_LOCATION=                           # optional, default us
GCP_PROCESSOR_ID=

# --- qwen-vl (self-hosted OpenAI-compatible endpoint, no data leaves your infra) ---
# The next line carries a real value, not a blank. On its own it marks qwen-vl configured.
QWEN_VL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000/v1
QWEN_VL_MODEL=                          # optional, default Qwen/Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct
QWEN_VL_API_KEY=                        # optional, only if your endpoint requires auth

# --- docling (self-hosted docling-serve container, no data leaves your infra) ---
# The next line carries a real value, not a blank. On its own it marks docling configured, and a
# scan under a `require_local` policy is then sent to this address.
DOCLING_SERVE_URL=http://localhost:5001

# ============================================================================================
# Operator knobs: every OPENREADING_* variable that changes how the system behaves rather than
# which vendor it talks to. All are commented out, and each entry names what unset does. The
# module that reads a knob owns its contract, and each block below points at that module. Two
# more modules read a knob without owning a block: openreading.cli.app returns exit 6 when an
# armed batch is interrupted, and openreading.router.compliance reads a self-hosted backend's
# address to check that a local backend really is local.
# ============================================================================================

# --- server deployment knobs (openreading serve) ---
# OPENREADING_MAX_BODY_BYTES=157286400             # raw HTTP request ceiling (150 MiB), including multipart framing
# OPENREADING_API_KEYS=                           # comma-separated bearer tokens for caller auth.
#                                                 #   Unset or empty leaves auth off, and every
#                                                 #   endpoint behaves as it does with zero
#                                                 #   configuration. An empty entry (a stray comma)
#                                                 #   fails startup, because a quietly dropped token
#                                                 #   would look configured when it is not.
#                                                 #   Configured, an unknown or absent bearer gets
#                                                 #   401 unauthorized
# OPENREADING_API_KEY_SCOPES=                     # comma-separated `token=backend1|backend2`
#                                                 #   entries, each narrowing one already-listed key
#                                                 #   to a backend allow-list. Unset leaves every
#                                                 #   key unscoped, and any malformed shape fails
#                                                 #   startup. A request for an out-of-scope backend
#                                                 #   gets 403 scope_denied, checked before any
#                                                 #   adapter is built
# OPENREADING_SERVER_PATH_ROOT=                   # directory a request's document.path may resolve
#                                                 #   beneath, checked per request by server/app.py
#                                                 #   `_gate_document_path`. Unset refuses every
#                                                 #   document.path, because HTTP turns a local
#                                                 #   field naming a file into a remote file-read
#                                                 #   primitive. The CLI and Python API ignore it
# OPENREADING_JOB_TTL_S=3600                      # seconds a terminal /v1/jobs record survives past
#                                                 #   its created_ms before the next store access
#                                                 #   sweeps it (M4). Unset = 1 hour
# OPENREADING_MAX_ASYNC_JOBS=1000                 # hard cap on /v1/jobs records in any state (M4).
#                                                 #   A submit at or over the cap is refused with
#                                                 #   429 rate_limited before its body is parsed.
#                                                 #   Unset = 1000
# OPENREADING_MAX_JOBS_PER_PRINCIPAL=100          # how many of those records one configured API key
#                                                 #   may hold, so the caller who fills the store
#                                                 #   cannot 429 everyone else. In force only when
#                                                 #   OPENREADING_API_KEYS is set. Unset = 100
# OPENREADING_ALLOW_UNSIGNED_WEBHOOKS=1           # accept a chunkr or open-ocr callback without the
#                                                 #   per-job token the server appended to the URL
#                                                 #   it registered, which leaves the vendor task id
#                                                 #   alone standing for proof. For a vendor that
#                                                 #   strips query parameters. Unset refuses it
#                                                 #   with 401
# OPENREADING_MAX_COMPARE_BYTES=8388608           # ceiling on a POST /v1/compare body, tighter than
#                                                 #   the transport cap because compare's cost is
#                                                 #   quadratic in the text it is given. Over it is
#                                                 #   400, never a truncated comparison.
#                                                 #   Unset = 8 MB

# --- document URL fetch (openreading.api._download) ---
# OPENREADING_ALLOW_PRIVATE_URLS=1                # allow a document URL whose host resolves to a
#                                                 #   private or loopback address, for an intranet
#                                                 #   store. Unset refuses one before the request
#                                                 #   leaves this process, which is what stops a
#                                                 #   caller-supplied URL from probing your internal
#                                                 #   network or cloud metadata service (SSRF).
#                                                 #   Every surface reads it, the CLI and the Python
#                                                 #   API included
# Full contract: uv run python -m pydoc openreading.api

# --- ledger execution plane (openreading parse / resume) ---
# OPENREADING_LEDGER=./.openreading               # directory path, and setting it arms the journal.
#                                                 #   The directory holds document payloads and the
#                                                 #   per-run keys that decrypt them. This repo's
#                                                 #   .gitignore covers `/.openreading/` at the
#                                                 #   clone root and nothing else, so any other path
#                                                 #   inside a clone needs its own ignore rule
#                                                 #   before you arm it. Only a strategy-dispatch
#                                                 #   run journals, so a named `--backend` writes
#                                                 #   nothing while appearing armed. Unset means no
#                                                 #   journal and no blob store
# Full contract: uv run python -m pydoc openreading.api

# --- the one file (openreading.yaml) ---
# OPENREADING_CONFIG=                             # explicit path to openreading.yaml, resolved by
#                                                 #   openreading.config and read by every command,
#                                                 #   not only strategy runs: its policy: block is
#                                                 #   the only place a compliance policy is
#                                                 #   written. Discovery order, first hit wins:
#                                                 #   --config or config=, then this var, then
#                                                 #   ./openreading.yaml. That last step is CLI and
#                                                 #   Python only, because the server never sniffs
#                                                 #   its cwd. Two files are never merged. With
#                                                 #   nothing found, no policy and no user-defined
#                                                 #   strategy loads
# OPENREADING_LLM_DECIDER=                        # second enablement key for the LLM decider.
#                                                 #   1/true/yes/on enables it, and a backend id
#                                                 #   both enables it and overrides
#                                                 #   `decider.llm.backend`. Unset means a
#                                                 #   configured decision downgrades to the engine
#                                                 #   default with reason `env_disabled`. The second
#                                                 #   key is deliberate, so that a checked-in YAML
#                                                 #   cannot start spending LLM tokens without
#                                                 #   operator consent at the env layer
# Full contract: uv run python -m pydoc openreading.strategies.decider

# --- credential broker ---
# OPENREADING_CREDENTIALS_REF_ALIASES=            # comma-separated env prefixes that a request's
#                                                 #   `credentials_ref: "env:<alias>"` is allowed to
#                                                 #   select. TEAM_A,TEAM_B lets `env:TEAM_A` read
#                                                 #   TEAM_A_API_KEY. Unset or empty accepts no
#                                                 #   alias at all, because a free-form prefix would
#                                                 #   let an unauthenticated request read any env
#                                                 #   var shaped <PREFIX>_<KEY>. Leave it unset
#                                                 #   unless you are deliberately exposing named
#                                                 #   credential slots to callers
# OPENREADING_TEXTRACT_S3_BUCKET is a backend setting, listed in the aws-textract block above.
# Full contract: uv run python -m pydoc openreading.credentials

# --- dev / test only ---
# `make verify-live` runs a backend's live tests when its variable is set, without checking the
# value. A stale hosted key fails loudly like any other auth error. QWEN_VL_ENDPOINT and
# DOCLING_SERVE_URL are addresses of local services rather than secrets, so a stale address makes
# the live test attempt a real connection instead of skipping. Comment those two lines out before
# `make verify-live` unless the service is running.
# OPENREADING_RECORD_FIXTURES=1                   # with `make verify-live`, also write
#                                                 #   secret-scrubbed real responses back into the
#                                                 #   offline fixtures, which is how mocks are
#                                                 #   refreshed after a vendor changes shape. The
#                                                 #   adapter checklist needs one such run through
#                                                 #   the CLI and one through the server. Never set
#                                                 #   it for an ordinary run, because it rewrites
#                                                 #   checked-in fixtures

# --- client side: read by scripts/upload_folder.py, never by openreading serve ---
# OPENREADING_API_KEY=                            # bearer token the folder recipe sends to your
#                                                 #   server. The server's own list is
#                                                 #   OPENREADING_API_KEYS above; this singular
#                                                 #   name does nothing for `openreading serve`

# --- not wired: nothing in src/ reads these, so setting one does nothing ---
# OPENREADING_DECIDER_EXECUTOR, OPENREADING_DECIDER_MODEL
#   Specified in internal/design/decider-executor.md, named in openreading.strategies.engine.
#   DECIDER_MODEL is the decider's own model selector, distinct from ANTHROPIC_MODEL, which
#   belongs to the parse adapter.
